  <data name="IntroductionV2NavigationTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start here</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2NavigationBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Devices page in the sidebar manages mice, keyboards, Blades, and headsets; Macros and Profiles are in the sidebar too.</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2DevicesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose a device</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2DevicesBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select a device card to open its settings. If nothing appears, select Rescan and check that the device is connected.</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2DeviceSettingsTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Device settings</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2MouseBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Adjust DPI, polling rate, lighting, and other supported options here; wireless mice also show battery level. Use Save or Apply on the relevant card; changes are not written automatically.</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2KeyboardBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Adjust lighting, polling rate, game mode, and other supported options here; wireless keyboards also show battery level. Use Save or Apply on the relevant card; changes are not written automatically.</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2BladeTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Blade settings</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2BladeBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Performance mode, fans, graphics mode, and keyboard lighting are on this page. Save or apply each change.</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2NoDevicesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>No devices found</value></data>
  <data name="IntroductionV2NoDevicesBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connect a Razer device, then select Rescan. If it still does not appear, check the USB or receiver connection; you can reopen this guide from Settings.</value></data>
